<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d69101bb28fce3cd7d7a0e73e74374509fa95923943eeefa7ad13f4a7707c9dd</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The dangers of revising Europe's security architecture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65bd77d48b864e5aaf1b7b133e3eb9202da7360fd8cade7d6ca02440f20523da</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049--ae25152ee718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn against revising Europe's security framework because they say it would mean granting Moscow its longstanding wish of renegotiating postwar security on the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest against public media reform plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a481525c2752470896ca2d300c2be5ff7e933d8c9d174f54baaeec72f15d05c</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533--a08ee7cdb27e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill to cut public media funding has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is planned for Prague on Sunday.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders tussle over whom to send to Ukraine, Russia peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:514d7893eb074531e4332d835f022089c45b58d0dbd1ae115c53f32c15863080</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468--127d08162dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A seat at the table for Europe now appears likely following comments by a US envoy who just held talks with Putin. But who will take that seat remains unclear.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can the EU make it harder to trick consumers online?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2924a3ffcc66eb0f2cd36c63857202f63cdd1da68c62bc86bbcab1b1d877a876</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447--856c99598d6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-the-eu-make-it-harder-to-trick-consumers-online/a-79933447?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants to curb subscription traps, misleading sales tactics and features that keep people scrolling. What would the proposed Digital Fairness Act change, and does it go far enough?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What have the talks with Russia and the US in Abu Dhabi achieved for Ukraine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae1ac89caae18aaa3513e845de82aa51b8602ea7a717d83aee50cd72cf623512</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613--89b8a9b8f641.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-have-the-talks-with-russia-and-the-us-in-abu-dhabi-achieved-for-ukraine/a-79930613?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The first trilateral talks between Ukraine, the US and Russia in nine months have ended with an agreement on exchanging prisoners. Does this mark a genuine breakthrough and a step toward peace?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary eases abortion restrictions in women's rights overhaul</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a73cc9799d764d2342e43643719756afa9da372af5326a78622085c6037a1136</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-rules/a-79931614--3bb42fe8feff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-eases-abortion-restrictions-in-women-s-rights-overhaul/a-79931614?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The reforms mark a break the the conservative policies of former PM Viktor Orban. The controversial "heartbeat regulation" is to be scrapped and women are to be better protected against violence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK court convicts 2 Iranian men of spying on journalists</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ddfa3c793b5855ce23773e5bf75424c9032d45ed6318d5724fefb352bd883d56</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583--9da85f420d5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-court-convicts-2-iranian-men-of-spying-on-journalists/a-79931583?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has found two Iranian citizens guilty of surveilling reporters for a Persian-language television station critical of Iran's government. One was also convicted of planning a violent attack against them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0c8e1ae31687e027e8ec015701119296dfd701fff57a62b93166c0127b11f1a</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British counterterrorism police arrest US soldier accused of spying on behalf of Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a20200d8016c6678d066f26394cc6328be6d2ef659e8ad1274b570436b678060</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240--5991e0a904a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-counterterrorism-police-arrest-us-soldier-accused-of-spying-on-behalf-of-russia/a-79913240?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A member of the US Army has been arrested near Gloucester in England. Police said he was suspected of espionage activity in connection with Russia. Investigators from the US and UK are involved in the probe.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK Privy Council overrules Trinidad and Tobago gay sex law</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23f3cb655cfd84f9e924c05d8355b23b234e2b29a05609e856fa41faa038bf7e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T19:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163--f186aba38925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-privy-council-overrules-trinidad-and-tobago-gay-sex-law/a-79912163?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A London court has overturned a Trinidad and Tobago law criminalizing consensual sexual relations between male same-sex couples. As a result of the colonial legacy, it is the independent country's last court of appeal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Victims of Nazi war in Poland call on Germany for support</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2da168206faf9b7f42074f174b73d21c34f9a7224f850cc417df24bb79beb79f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T17:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311--36756d6320e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/victims-of-nazi-war-in-poland-call-on-germany-for-support/a-79909311?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 80 years after the end of World War II, Polish victims of the Nazi regime are still waiting for a "humanitarian gesture" from Germany. The 2027 draft budget hasn't left them much hope for possible reparations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran denies role in fridge hack, France summons ambassador</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f46dbdfe588369e4ecfb1491184df28096676b61e9014192d4644eecb0b73bd</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206--6d0355211a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-denies-role-in-fridge-hack-france-summons-ambassador/a-79910206?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">France has said it rules "nothing" out in response to a cyberattack on supermarket refrigeration units. Iran, however, said it categorically rejected Paris' "baseless and one-sided accusations" of IRGC involvement.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria highway pileup kills 12, dozens injured: PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c071ddf1c2155c72ea9264d37f6e0928269be14f7ae9f8abf3178bc261729f16</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978--e4c51329b4c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-highway-pileup-kills-12-dozens-injured-pm/a-79907978?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least 12 people were killed and dozens injured in a series of crashes caused by thick fog in Bulgaria. Police, firefighters and paramedics were dispatched to the scene for the rescue operation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Online disinformation rife after Krakow mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:641e3b5439022f827653d5dc482dda7fec34d66b6294a4aab4900073753c00e1</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620--80ad1afffb68.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-online-disinformation-rife-after-krakow-mass-shooting/a-79900620?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fake and AI-manipulated images spread online in the hours after the Krakow attack, fueling false narratives about the mass shooting. DW Fact Check examined what's real, and what isn't.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US, Russia, Ukraine wrap up talks with prisoner exchange agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e175d4bfd52b748b4ba03819bd97e8cccad94fd3394b62c054cfb811ea5d43f</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T07:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-russia-ukraine-wrap-up-talks-with-prisoner-exchange-agreement/live-79906232--00cfe2e7daba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-russia-ukraine-wrap-up-talks-with-prisoner-exchange-agreement/live-79906232?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Peace talks between Russia, Ukraine and the US concluded in the United Arab Emirates. The two day talks were the first such meeting since February. DW has the latest updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New trilateral talks on Ukraine war in Abu Dhabi: What to expect?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f0681406933af3d4dde98bc1f4a26864d82b7fa297d6cab7acafd98ab2073b1</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T23:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734--3c6da76b72e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-trilateral-talks-on-ukraine-war-in-abu-dhabi-what-to-expect/a-79905734?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian and Russian representatives last met in February for talks on ending the war, but the same sticking points remain. Ukraine continues to demand security guarantees, which is a non-starter for Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Independent Novaya Gazeta shuts its Moscow newsroom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2df9980e54eebe03c053680c17605e82d3af9b8a4093eb57cd25d50cd3597960</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T16:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827--d187f3fbc3fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-independent-novaya-gazeta-shuts-its-moscow-newsroom/a-79899827?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The investigative newspaper is closing its doors after Russian authorities labeled it a "foreign agent" and ordered it vacate its Moscow premises.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU aims to pick new ECB chief by year-end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4993ef9f18b350c6885e054f03f709a841bcdaf3668531418471a4103f209f77</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169--04bae0a2e38e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-aims-to-pick-new-ecb-chief-by-year-end/a-79898169?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christine Lagarde's decision to step down early as head of the European Central Bank (ECB) has put the European Union on a tight schedule. The bloc expects to pick a new ECB chief by the end of December.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Krakow mass shooting suspect has died in hospital, police in Poland say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:271eac8d5f6004771e2ddb754c369967eb53ce8b072a4176447a55a21fa007e0</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T06:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/krakow-mass-shooting-suspect-has-died-in-hospital-police-in-poland-say/a-79895626--6dfb07803fa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/krakow-mass-shooting-suspect-has-died-in-hospital-police-in-poland-say/a-79895626?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The alleged gunman who killed six people in a shooting spree in the Polish city of Krakow has died of injuries sustained in a shootout with police, authorities say.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
